---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-ai-badge</code> is the one marker for anything the assistant made that a person hasn't
  accepted yet. Peacock's AI rules (ADR-030002, after Redvars ADR-000007) ask that AI output is
  visible as such, says why, and can be cleared in one action; this badge does all three.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center;'>
    <wc-ai-badge></wc-ai-badge>
    <wc-ai-badge kind='draft'></wc-ai-badge>
    <wc-ai-badge kind='generated'></wc-ai-badge>
    <wc-ai-badge kind='generated'>Summary by the assistant</wc-ai-badge>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Kinds</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>suggested</code> (default): a value the person hasn't accepted, such as a field the assistant filled in.</li>
  <li><code>draft</code>: a record or text waiting to be confirmed, such as an incident the assistant prepared.</li>
  <li><code>generated</code>: read-only output, such as a summary. It shows as colored text without a container.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Saying why</h3>
<p>
  <code>reason</code> is one sentence on why the assistant chose this. It shows in a tooltip on hover
  or keyboard focus, and screen readers read it as the badge's description.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <p style='display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center;'>
    Urgency: 3 · Medium
    <wc-ai-badge reason="You didn't say you can't work. Make it High if you can't."></wc-ai-badge>
  </p>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Clearing in one action</h3>
<p>
  <code>dismissible</code> adds a clear button. It fires <code>dismiss</code>; the app then removes the
  suggestion, discards the draft or hides the summary. The button is named for the kind: "Clear
  suggestion", "Discard draft" or "Hide".
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center;'>
    <wc-ai-badge id='ai-badge-dismiss' dismissible reason='Assigned to you in Asset management.'></wc-ai-badge>
    <wc-ai-badge kind='draft' dismissible></wc-ai-badge>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#ai-badge-dismiss').addEventListener('dismiss', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('dismiss');
      event.target.hidden = true;
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Icon only</h3>
<p>
  <code>icon-only</code> keeps just the sparkle where there is no room for the label. The label is
  still read by screen readers and shows in the tooltip, before the reason. Fields switch to it on
  their own: a text field narrower than 20rem, and a textarea always, since a label beside it would
  narrow every line of the text.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center;'>
    <wc-ai-badge icon-only reason='Matches the caller’s site.'></wc-ai-badge>
    <wc-ai-badge icon-only dismissible></wc-ai-badge>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>When AI is off</h3>
<p>
  When the page turns AI off, every badge renders nothing, so a page that still passes AI state in
  never shows a stale marker (<a href='/ai/'>AI setup</a> explains the settings):
</p>

<pre><code>import {'{ setPeacockAi }'} from '@redvars/peacock';

// The instance turned the assistant off.
setPeacockAi({'{ enabled: false }'});</code></pre>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  The label is always text, never only the color or the sparkle, which is hidden from screen readers.
  With a reason, the label is focusable so keyboard users can reach the tooltip. The labels are Peacock
  strings (<code>aiSuggested</code>, <code>aiDraft</code>, <code>aiGenerated</code>,
  <code>aiClearSuggestion</code>, <code>aiDiscardDraft</code>, <code>aiHideGenerated</code>) and can be
  translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>.
</p>
